      "taskType": "application",
      "prompt": "A rectangular display must keep the same area. One design is {{l1}} inches long and {{w1}} inches wide. Let w be width and l be length. Recognize the inverse variation, determine the constant area, formulate w as a function of l, and find the width when the length is {{l2}} inches.",
      "stimulus": {
        "kind": "table",
        "title": "Fixed-area design",
        "table": {
          "headers": [
            "Length l (in)",
            "Width w (in)",
            "Area lw (in²)"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "{{l1}}",
              "{{w1}}",
              "?"
            ],
            [
              "{{l2}}",
              "?",
              "same constant"
            ]
          ]
        }
      },
      "responseFields": [
        {
          "id": "constant",
          "label": "Constant area k",
          "inputProfile": "number",
          "unit": "square inches",
          "expected": "{{area}}"
        },
        {
          "id": "equation",
          "label": "Inverse-variation width model",
          "inputProfile": "equation",
          "equivalence": "modelEquation",
          "expected": "w={{area}}/l"
        },
        {
          "id": "prediction",
          "label": "Width when l={{l2}}",
          "inputProfile": "number",
          "unit": "inches",
          "expected": "{{w2}}"
        }
      ],
      "solutionReview": {
        "headline": "For fixed area, length and width vary inversely.",
        "reasoning": [
          "The constant product is lw=({{l1}})({{w1}})={{area}}.",
          "Solving for width gives w={{area}}/l.",
          "At l={{l2}}, the width is {{w2}} inches."
        ],
        "answerSummary": "w={{area}}/l and w={{w2}} inches when l={{l2}}."
      },
      "attemptFeedback": [
        "A constant product signals inverse variation; use the first design to determine that constant."
      ],
      "supportHints": [
        "Rectangle area is l·w. If area stays fixed, l·w=k."
      ],
      "generator": {
        "parameters": {
          "l1": {
            "type": "int",
            "min": 4,
            "max": 15
          },
          "w1": {
            "type": "int",
            "min": 4,
            "max": 15
          },
          "l2": {
            "type": "int",
            "min": 4,
            "max": 18
          }
        },
        "derived": {
          "area": "l1*w1",
          "w2": "area/l2"
        },
        "constraints": [
          "l2!=l1",
          "area%l2==0"
        ],
        "attempts": 300
      }
    },
