        {
          "id": "equation",
          "label": "Correct inverse-variation equation",
          "inputProfile": "equation",
          "equivalence": "modelEquation",
          "expected": "y={{k}}/x"
        },
        {
          "id": "prediction",
          "label": "Correct y when x={{x2}}",
          "inputProfile": "number",
          "expected": "{{y2}}"
        }
      ],
      "solutionReview": {
        "headline": "Inverse variation uses a constant product, not a constant ratio.",
        "reasoning": [
          "The student treated the relationship as direct variation.",
          "For inverse variation, k=xy=({{x1}})({{y1}})={{k}}, so y={{k}}/x.",
          "At x={{x2}}, y={{y2}}."
        ],
        "answerSummary": "The corrected model is y={{k}}/x and the requested value is {{y2}}."
